content:
I'll start by exploring the workspace and understanding the data files.

```json
{
  "tool": "list_files",
  "args": {}
}
```

Now let me read the data files to understand what we're working with.

```json
{
  "tool": "read_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "data/analysis_spec.txt"
  }
}
```

Now let me read the radiocarbon measurements data.

```json
{
  "tool": "read_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "data/radiocarbon_measurements.csv"
  }
}
```

Now I need to understand the workspace structure and create necessary directories. Let me first list all files to see the current structure.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "dir /s /b"
  }
}
```

I need to create the required directory structure: code/, outputs/, report/, and report/images/. Let me create these directories.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "mkdir code outputs report report\\images"
  }
}
```

Now let me run the analysis script to generate results and figures.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "cd code && python radiocarbon_analysis.py"
  }
}
```

Great! The analysis ran successfully. Now I need to check if the outputs were created and then work on the calibration to calendar years. The task mentions "calibrated calendar per sample" - I need to implement calibration. Let me first check what outputs were created.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "dir outputs"
  }
}
```

Now let me check the report/images directory to see if figures were created.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "dir report\\images"
  }
}
```

Now let me run the calibration analysis.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "cd code && python calibration_analysis.py"
  }
}
```

Now I need to create the final report. Let me first check all the outputs and figures that have been created, then write the comprehensive report.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "dir report\\images"
  }
}
```

Good! Now let me read the calibrated results to include in the report.

```json
{
  "tool": "read_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "outputs/calibrated_results.csv"
  }
}
```

Now let me verify that the report file exists and check its content briefly.

```json
{
  "tool": "read_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "report/report.md"
  }
}
```

Perfect! The report looks comprehensive and includes all required elements. Now let me make sure all deliverables are complete by checking the final directory structure.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "dir /s /b"
  }
}
```
